IMPORT prelude

-- Motor Vehicles (Third-Party Risks and Compensation) Act 1960 (Singapore) -- whether I must have third-party cover and
-- whether the cover I have counts (ss 3, 3A, 4), what my insurer cannot use against the person I injure (ss 5, 7, 8, 14),
-- when my insurer must pay a judgment against me and what it can then claw back from me (s 9), what my bankruptcy does
-- (ss 10, 12, 13), and the duties the Act puts on me: to say whether I was insured (s 11), to surrender my certificate
-- (s 15), and to produce it and report an injury accident (s 16), with the penalties.
--
-- SEAT: the driver or owner of a motor vehicle -- the person who uses it, or causes or permits another to use it, on a road.
-- Every decision is phrased as that person would ask it. Where a provision addresses only the insurer, the court or the
-- police, it is encoded as what it means for the driver or owner.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 2 ("motor vehicle", "relevant amount", "road", "specified person" para (b), "use"); s 3(1)-(4),
-- (6), (7); s 3A(1); s 4(1), (4), (9), (11), (12); s 5; s 7; s 8(1), (3); s 9(1), (6), (7), (8), (9), (14) ("liability
-- covered by the terms of the policy"); s 10(1), (2), (6); s 11(1), (6); s 12; s 13(1); s 14(1); s 15; s 16(1)-(8).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 January 2026 (carrying Act 30 of 2024 on platform
-- workers, in force 1 January 2025, and Act 2 of 2025 on disqualification, in force 1 January 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/MVTPRCA1960.txt.
--
-- NUMBERS SET ELSEWHERE. The "relevant amount" is $5,000 "or, where another amount has been prescribed under section 20",
-- the prescribed amount. No order under s 20 is deposited, so the relevant amount is an INPUT to every rule that uses it;
-- the cases supply 5000, the figure in s 2.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 4(2), (3) (policies issued on or before 21 October 1998); s 4(5)-(7) (the insurer's or owner's payment
-- of hospital expenses, capped at $400 in-patient and $40 outpatient); ss 5A, 6 (settlement agreements and payment to the
-- Public Trustee); s 9(2)-(5), (10)-(13) (costs, and the Public Trustee's handling of the money); s 10(3)-(5); s 11(2)-(5)
-- (the information duties of a trustee in bankruptcy, liquidator or insurer); s 14(2) (the policy survives my death -- a
-- single sentence with no condition, noted below); s 17 (deposits); s 18 (solicitation of claims); ss 18A-24 (the Public
-- Trustee's powers, the power to amend sums, securities, the general penalty, the Minister's power to exempt, rules).
-- Who is liable to the injured person at all (negligence) is the general law and is not decided here.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Motor Vehicles (Third-Party Risks and Compensation) Act 1960`

§§ `3. Users of motor vehicles to be insured against third-party risks`

-- s 2: "'use' means use on any road"; "'road' means any public road and any other road to which the public has access".
-- s 3(1): "it is not lawful for any person to use or to cause or permit any other person to use -- (a) a motor vehicle in
-- Singapore; or (b) a motor vehicle which is registered in Singapore in any territory specified in the Schedule, unless
-- there is in force in relation to the use ... a policy of insurance or a security in respect of third-party risks that
-- complies with the requirements of this Act."
-- The Schedule ("Territory") as deposited names West Malaysia; the page layout is garbled, so the territory is named here
-- by reference to the Schedule rather than by name.
DECLARE `Where the vehicle is used` IS ONE OF
    `on a road in Singapore`                                                      -- s 3(1)(a)
    `on a road in a territory in the Schedule, the vehicle being registered in Singapore` -- s 3(1)(b)
    `somewhere section 3 does not reach`                                          -- off-road, or abroad elsewhere

-- s 3(6): "This section does not apply -- (a) to a vehicle owned by -- (i) the Government; (ii) the government of Malaysia
-- or of any State of Malaysia; or (iii) any visiting forces ..., on any occasion upon which the vehicle is being used by any
-- person authorised by any of such governments or by any such forces ...; (b) to a vehicle owned by a person who has
-- deposited and keeps deposited with the Accountant-General the sum of $125,000 at any time when the vehicle is being driven
-- by the owner or by an employee of the owner in the course of his or her employment or is otherwise subject to the control
-- of the owner; or (c) to any vehicle at any time when it is being driven for police purposes by or under the direction of
-- (i) a police officer ... or (ii) the Registrar ...". s 3(7): "This section does not extend to invalid carriages."
-- The occasion is one choice because the exemptions are alternatives; an ordinary private use is the first.
DECLARE `The vehicle and the occasion` IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary use of an ordinary vehicle`
    `a Government, Malaysian or visiting forces vehicle used by a person they authorised`     -- s 3(6)(a)
    `the vehicle of an owner keeping $125,000 deposited, driven by the owner or an employee at work or under the owner's control` -- s 3(6)(b)
    `a vehicle driven for police purposes by or under the direction of a police officer or the Registrar` -- s 3(6)(c)
    `an invalid carriage`                                                                    -- s 3(7)

-- s 4(1): "a policy of insurance must ... be a policy which -- (a) is issued by an insurer who at the time the policy is
-- issued is lawfully carrying on motor insurance business in Singapore; and (b) insures the person ... in respect of any
-- liability which may be incurred ... in respect of the death of or bodily injury to any person caused by or arising out of
-- the use of the motor vehicle". s 4(9): "A policy is of no effect for the purposes of this Act unless there is issued by
-- the insurer to the person by whom the policy is effected a certificate (called in this Act a certificate of insurance)".
-- s 2: "'policy of insurance' includes a cover note".
DECLARE `My policy` HAS
    `in force for this use`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `issued by an insurer lawfully carrying on motor insurance business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 4(1)(a), at issue
    `insuring against liability for death or bodily injury to any person from the use` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 4(1)(b)
    `a certificate of insurance was issued for it`                                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 4(9)

-- s 4(11): a security "must -- (a) be given either by an insurer approved by the Minister or by some body of persons
-- approved by the Minister ...; and (b) consist of an undertaking ... to make good ... up to the amount in the case of an
-- undertaking relating to the use of public service vehicles of not less than $225,000 and in any other case of not less
-- than $45,000". s 4(12): no effect "unless there is issued ... a certificate (called in this Act a certificate of
-- security)". "Public service vehicle" is a Road Traffic Act term, asked as a fact.
DECLARE `My security` HAS
    `in force for the use`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `given by an insurer or body approved by the Minister`       IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 4(11)(a)
    `the amount of the undertaking in dollars`                   IS A NUMBER   -- s 4(11)(b)
    `a certificate of security was issued for it`                IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 4(12)

-- s 3(4): "A person shall not be guilty of an offence under this section if the person proves -- (a) that the motor
-- vehicle did not belong to the person and was not in the person's possession under a contract of hiring or loan; (b) that
-- the person was using the vehicle in the course of the person's employment; and (c) that the person neither knew nor had
-- reason to believe that there was not in force ... a policy of insurance or such security as complies ...".
-- "if the person proves": each limb is phrased as what I can prove.
DECLARE `My use` HAS
    `where`                                                                          IS A `Where the vehicle is used`
    `the occasion`                                                                   IS A `The vehicle and the occasion`
    `a public service vehicle`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the policy`                                                                     IS A `My policy`
    `the security`                                                                   IS A `My security`
    `I can prove the vehicle was not mine and not with me on hire or loan`           IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 3(4)(a)
    `I can prove I was using it in the course of my employment`                      IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 3(4)(b)
    `I can prove I neither knew nor had reason to believe there was no complying cover` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 3(4)(c)

GIVEN `the policy` IS A `My policy`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my policy comply with the requirements of this Act` IF
        `the policy`'s `issued by an insurer lawfully carrying on motor insurance business in Singapore`
    AND `the policy`'s `insuring against liability for death or bodily injury to any person from the use`
    AND `the policy`'s `a certificate of insurance was issued for it`

GIVEN `the security` IS A `My security`, `a public service vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my security comply with the requirements of this Act` IF
        `the security`'s `given by an insurer or body approved by the Minister`
    AND `the security`'s `the amount of the undertaking in dollars` AT LEAST `the minimum undertaking in dollars`
    AND `the security`'s `a certificate of security was issued for it`
    WHERE
        `the minimum undertaking in dollars` MEANS IF `a public service vehicle` THEN 225000 ELSE 45000

GIVEN `the use` IS A `My use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 3 require cover for my use` IF
        `the use reaches section 3`
    AND `the occasion is not exempt`
    WHERE
        `the use reaches section 3` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the use`'s `where`
            WHEN `somewhere section 3 does not reach` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE
        `the occasion is not exempt` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the use`'s `the occasion`
            WHEN `an ordinary use of an ordinary vehicle` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the use` IS A `My use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is complying cover in force for my use` IF
        (    `the use`'s `the policy`'s `in force for this use`
         AND `Does my policy comply with the requirements of this Act` (`the use`'s `the policy`))
    OR  (    `the use`'s `the security`'s `in force for the use`
         AND `Does my security comply with the requirements of this Act` (`the use`'s `the security`) (`the use`'s `a public service vehicle`))

GIVEN `the use` IS A `My use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I make out the employed driver's defence` IF
        `the use`'s `I can prove the vehicle was not mine and not with me on hire or loan`
    AND `the use`'s `I can prove I was using it in the course of my employment`
    AND `the use`'s `I can prove I neither knew nor had reason to believe there was no complying cover`

-- s 3(2): "If a person acts in contravention of this section, the person shall be guilty of an offence".
GIVEN `the use` IS A `My use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of an offence by using the vehicle without cover` IF
        `Does section 3 require cover for my use` `the use`
    AND NOT `Is complying cover in force for my use` `the use`
    AND NOT `Can I make out the employed driver's defence` `the use`

-- s 3(3): "A person convicted of an offence under this section is (unless the court for special reasons thinks fit to order
-- otherwise and without affecting the power of the court to order a longer period of disqualification) to be disqualified
-- from holding or obtaining a driving licence under the Road Traffic Act 1961 for a period of 12 months starting on the date
-- of the person's conviction or, if the person is sentenced to imprisonment, on the date of the person's release from
-- prison."  [Act 2 of 2025 wef 01/01/2026]
-- "special reasons" is the court's judgment, so it is an input; the answer is the period the Act fixes, a minimum because
-- the court may order longer.
GIVEN `the court for special reasons orders otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `For how many months at least must I be disqualified from driving after a section 3 conviction` IS
    IF `the court for special reasons orders otherwise` THEN 0 ELSE 12

DECLARE `When the disqualification starts` IS ONE OF
    `on the date of my conviction`
    `on the date of my release from prison`

GIVEN `I am sentenced to imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `When the disqualification starts`
DECIDE `When does my disqualification start` IS
    IF `I am sentenced to imprisonment` THEN `on the date of my release from prison` ELSE `on the date of my conviction`

§§ `3A. Presumption as to using motor vehicle`

-- s 3A(1): "it is presumed, until the contrary is proved, that a person uses a motor vehicle on a road in Singapore if it is
-- proved -- (a) for a vehicle registered under the Road Traffic Act 1961, that the person is, at the material time, recorded
-- as the owner ...; (b) for a vehicle the registration of which ... is cancelled ... or has lapsed, that the person is last
-- recorded as the owner ...; or (c) for a vehicle that is not registered ... that the person has a legal right to possession
-- of the vehicle (including any person who has the use of the vehicle under a lease or hire-purchase agreement, but not the
-- lessor while the vehicle is being leased under any such agreement)."
DECLARE `How I stand to the vehicle` IS ONE OF
    `the recorded owner of a registered vehicle`                                      -- (a)
    `the last recorded owner of a vehicle whose registration was cancelled or lapsed` -- (b)
    `entitled to possession of an unregistered vehicle, including as lessee or hirer` -- (c)
    `the lessor of an unregistered vehicle while it is leased out`                    -- (c), the exception
    `none of these`

GIVEN `how I stand` IS A `How I stand to the vehicle`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I presumed to be using the vehicle on a road in Singapore` IF
    CONSIDER `how I stand`
    WHEN `the lessor of an unregistered vehicle while it is leased out` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `4(4). What my policy need not cover`

-- s 4(4): "A policy of insurance is not, by virtue of subsection (1)(b), required to cover -- (a) liability in respect of --
-- (i) the death of or bodily injury sustained by a person (A) who is in the employment of a person insured by the policy,
-- where the death or bodily injury arises out of and in the course of A's employment; or (ii) the death of or bodily injury
-- sustained by a platform worker (B) who provides a platform service for a platform operator insured by the policy, where
-- the death or bodily injury arises out of and in the course of B's provision of the platform service ...; or (b) any
-- contractual liability."  [(a)(ii) Act 30 of 2024 wef 01/01/2025]
-- s 4(4A) borrows "platform operator", "platform service" and "platform worker" from the Platform Workers Act 2024: facts.
DECLARE `The injury` HAS
    `death or bodily injury caused by or arising out of the use of the vehicle`         IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 4(1)(b)
    `to someone employed by a person insured by the policy`                             IS A BOOLEAN  -- (4)(a)(i) status
    `arising out of and in the course of that employment`                               IS A BOOLEAN  -- (4)(a)(i) occasion
    `to a platform worker providing a platform service for a platform operator insured by the policy` IS A BOOLEAN -- (4)(a)(ii)
    `arising out of and in the course of providing that platform service`               IS A BOOLEAN  -- (4)(a)(ii)
    `a contractual liability`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN  -- (4)(b)

GIVEN `the injury` IS A `The injury`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my policy cover my liability for this death or injury` IF
        `the injury`'s `death or bodily injury caused by or arising out of the use of the vehicle`
    AND NOT `section 4(4) takes it outside the required cover`
    WHERE
        `section 4(4) takes it outside the required cover` MEANS
                (    `the injury`'s `to someone employed by a person insured by the policy`
                 AND `the injury`'s `arising out of and in the course of that employment`)
            OR  (    `the injury`'s `to a platform worker providing a platform service for a platform operator insured by the policy`
                 AND `the injury`'s `arising out of and in the course of providing that platform service`)
            OR  `the injury`'s `a contractual liability`

§§ `5. Agreements with my passenger`

-- s 5(1): where s 3 requires cover for my use and "any other person is carried in or upon the motor vehicle ..., any
-- antecedent agreement or understanding between them (whether intended to be legally binding or not) is of no effect so far
-- as it purports or might be held -- (a) to negative or restrict any such liability of the user ... as is required by
-- section 4 to be covered ...; or (b) to impose any conditions with respect to the enforcement of any such liability".
-- s 5(2): "The fact that a person so carried ... has willingly accepted as the person's the risk of negligence on the part
-- of the user is not to be treated as negativing any such liability of the user."
-- s 5(3): carried includes "entering or getting on to, or alighting from"; an antecedent agreement is "one made at any time
-- before the liability arose".
DECLARE `My passenger` HAS
    `section 3 required cover for my use`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `carried in or on the vehicle, or getting in, on or out`                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 5(3)
    `we had an agreement or understanding, binding or not`                       IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 5(1)
    `made before the liability arose`                                            IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 5(3)
    `it restricts my liability or puts conditions on enforcing it`               IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 5(1)(a), (b)

GIVEN `the passenger` IS A `My passenger`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my agreement with my passenger of no effect` IF
        `the passenger`'s `section 3 required cover for my use`
    AND `the passenger`'s `carried in or on the vehicle, or getting in, on or out`
    AND `the passenger`'s `we had an agreement or understanding, binding or not`
    AND `the passenger`'s `made before the liability arose`
    AND `the passenger`'s `it restricts my liability or puts conditions on enforcing it`

-- s 5(2) answers only where s 5 applies -- s 3 required cover and the person was carried. Elsewhere the general law of
-- volenti decides, which this encoding does not cover: the answer says so rather than guessing.
DECLARE `What my passenger's acceptance of the risk does` IS ONE OF
    `it does not negative my liability (section 5(2))`
    `not covered by this encoding: section 5 does not apply, so the general law decides`

GIVEN `the passenger` IS A `My passenger`
GIVETH A `What my passenger's acceptance of the risk does`
DECIDE `Does my passenger's willing acceptance of the risk negative my liability` IS
    IF      `the passenger`'s `section 3 required cover for my use`
        AND `the passenger`'s `carried in or on the vehicle, or getting in, on or out`
    THEN `it does not negative my liability (section 5(2))`
    ELSE `not covered by this encoding: section 5 does not apply, so the general law decides`

§§ `7 and 8. Conditions and restrictions in my policy`

-- s 7(1): "Any condition in a policy ... providing that no liability arises under the policy ... or that any liability so
-- arising ceases in the event of some specified thing being done or omitted to be done after the happening of the event
-- giving rise to a claim ... is of no effect in connection with such claims as are mentioned in section 4(1)(b)."
-- s 7(2): "Nothing in this section is taken to render void any provision in a policy ... requiring the person insured ... to
-- repay to the insurer ... any sums which the latter may have become liable to pay ... and which have been applied to the
-- satisfaction of the claims of third parties."
GIVEN `the condition cuts off cover for something done or not done after the accident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is one section 4(1)(b) requires to be covered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my policy condition of no effect against the person I injured` IF
        `the condition cuts off cover for something done or not done after the accident`
    AND `the claim is one section 4(1)(b) requires to be covered`

GIVEN `my policy requires me to repay sums applied to third-party claims` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my insurer make me repay what it paid the person I injured under section 7` IF
    `my policy requires me to repay sums applied to third-party claims`

-- s 8(1): where a certificate of insurance has been issued, "so much of the policy as purports to restrict the insurance
-- ... by reference to any of the following matters" is, as respects the s 4(1)(b) liabilities, "of no effect": (a) the age
-- or physical or mental condition of persons driving the vehicle; (b) the condition of the vehicle; (c) the number of
-- persons that the vehicle carries; (d) the weight or physical characteristics of the goods; (e) the times at which or the
-- areas within which the vehicle is used; (f) the horsepower or value; (g) the carrying of any particular apparatus;
-- (h) the carrying of any particular means of identification other than one required by the Road Traffic Act 1961.
-- A closed list: a restriction on any other ground stands.
-- s 8(3): "Any sum paid by an insurer ... which is covered by the policy by virtue only of this section is recoverable by
-- the insurer from that person."
DECLARE `Ground of the restriction` IS ONE OF
    `the age or physical or mental condition of persons driving the vehicle`             -- (a)
    `the condition of the vehicle`                                                       -- (b)
    `the number of persons that the vehicle carries`                                     -- (c)
    `the weight or physical characteristics of the goods that the vehicle carries`      -- (d)
    `the times at which or the areas within which the vehicle is used`                   -- (e)
    `the horsepower or value of the vehicle`                                             -- (f)
    `the carrying on the vehicle of any particular apparatus`                            -- (g)
    `the carrying of a means of identification the Road Traffic Act 1961 does not require` -- (h)
    `a ground outside the section 8(1) list`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A `Ground of the restriction`
      `a certificate of insurance was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability is one section 4(1)(b) requires to be covered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my policy's restriction of no effect against the person I injured` IF
        `a certificate of insurance was issued`
    AND `the liability is one section 4(1)(b) requires to be covered`
    AND `the ground is on the list`
    WHERE
        `the ground is on the list` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the ground`
            WHEN `a ground outside the section 8(1) list` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the sum was covered by the policy only because of section 8` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my insurer recover from me what it paid only because of section 8` IF
    `the sum was covered by the policy only because of section 8`

§§ `9. Duty of insurers to satisfy judgments against persons insured`

-- s 2 "specified person", para (b): "for the purposes of section 9, a person who is entitled to the benefit of a judgment
-- referred to in section 9(1)(b) and who, at the time the judgment is given -- (i) is below 21 years of age; (ii) lacks
-- capacity within the meaning of section 4 of the Mental Capacity Act 2008; (iii) is not represented by a public officer or
-- an advocate and solicitor; (iv) is isolated in a hospital or other place under section 15(1) or (2) of the Infectious
-- Diseases Act 1976; or (v) is under legal custody in a place of detention". Borrowed terms (capacity, isolation, place of
-- detention) are facts.
DECLARE `The person I injured` HAS
    `age in years when judgment was given`                                    IS A NUMBER   -- (b)(i)
    `lacking capacity under the Mental Capacity Act 2008 when judgment was given` IS A BOOLEAN -- (b)(ii)
    `unrepresented by a public officer or advocate and solicitor when judgment was given` IS A BOOLEAN -- (b)(iii)
    `isolated under the Infectious Diseases Act 1976 when judgment was given` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(iv)
    `in legal custody in a place of detention when judgment was given`       IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(v)

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A `The person I injured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the person I injured a specified person` IF
        `the claimant`'s `age in years when judgment was given` LESS THAN 21
    OR  `the claimant`'s `lacking capacity under the Mental Capacity Act 2008 when judgment was given`
    OR  `the claimant`'s `unrepresented by a public officer or advocate and solicitor when judgment was given`
    OR  `the claimant`'s `isolated under the Infectious Diseases Act 1976 when judgment was given`
    OR  `the claimant`'s `in legal custody in a place of detention when judgment was given`

-- s 9(6)(c): "if before the happening of the event which was the cause of the death or bodily injury ... the policy was
-- cancelled by mutual consent or by virtue of any provision contained in the policy and either -- (i) before the happening of
-- that event the certificate was surrendered to the insurer or the person to whom the certificate was issued made a
-- statutory declaration stating that the certificate had been lost or destroyed; (ii) after the happening of that event but
-- before the end of a period of 14 days from the taking effect of the cancellation of the policy the certificate was
-- surrendered ... or ... such a statutory declaration ...; or (iii) before or after the happening of that event but within
-- the period of 14 days the insurer commenced proceedings under this Act in respect of the failure to surrender".
DECLARE `What became of the certificate after cancellation` IS ONE OF
    `surrendered or declared lost before the accident`                                         -- (i)
    `surrendered or declared lost after the accident, within 14 days of the cancellation taking effect` -- (ii)
    `the insurer sued over its non-surrender within 14 days of the cancellation taking effect` -- (iii)
    `none of these`

-- s 9(1): "if after a certificate of insurance has been issued ... judgment in respect of any liability required to be
-- covered by a policy under section 4(1)(b) (being a liability covered by the terms of the policy) is obtained against any
-- person insured by the policy, then, even though the insurer may be entitled to avoid or cancel or may have avoided or
-- cancelled the policy," the insurer (a) MAY pay where the sum (excluding costs and judgment interest) "does not exceed the
-- relevant amount"; (b) MUST pay where it "exceeds the relevant amount", "directly to -- (i) the Public Trustee as trustee
-- for the person if the person is a specified person and the judgment requires the sum to be paid to the Public Trustee as
-- trustee for the person; or (ii) in any other case, the person".
-- s 9(14): "'liability covered by the terms of the policy' means a liability which is covered by the policy or which would
-- be so covered but for the fact that the insurer is entitled to avoid or cancel or has avoided or cancelled the policy".
-- s 9(6): "No sum is payable by an insurer under subsections (1) and (4) -- (a) ... unless before or within 7 days after the
-- commencement of the proceedings in which the judgment was given the insurer had notice of the bringing of the
-- proceedings; (b) ... so long as enforcement on the judgment is stayed pending an appeal; or (c)" as above.
-- s 9(7): nothing is payable if, "in an action commenced before or within 3 months after the commencement of the
-- proceedings in which the judgment was given", the insurer has obtained a declaration that it is entitled to avoid the
-- policy for non-disclosure of a material fact or a materially false representation.
-- s 9(8): an insurer with such a declaration does not get the benefit of s 9(7) for a judgment in proceedings begun BEFORE
-- its action "unless before or within 7 days after the commencement of that action the insurer has given notice thereof to
-- the person who is the claimant in those proceedings specifying the non-disclosure or false representation".
-- Whether the court has granted the declaration is the court's judgment: an input.
DECLARE `The judgment against me` HAS
    `the claimant`                                                                    IS A `The person I injured`
    `the injury`                                                                      IS A `The injury`
    `a certificate of insurance had been issued for my policy`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the liability is covered by my policy, or would be but for the insurer's right to avoid or cancel it` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 9(14)
    `I am a person insured by the policy`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sum awarded, excluding costs and interest, in dollars`                       IS A NUMBER
    `the judgment requires payment to the Public Trustee`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 9(6)(a): days after the proceedings began on which the insurer had notice of them; 0 or less if before;
    -- NOTHING if it never had notice.
    `days after the proceedings began that my insurer had notice of them`             IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `enforcement is stayed pending an appeal`                                         IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 9(6)(b)
    `my policy was cancelled before the accident`                                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 9(6)(c)
    `the certificate`                                                                 IS A `What became of the certificate after cancellation`
    `the court has declared, in an action begun no later than 3 months after the proceedings, that my insurer may avoid the policy for non-disclosure or misrepresentation` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 9(7)
    `the proceedings against me began before the insurer's action`                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 9(8)
    `my insurer told the claimant of its action, and the ground, within 7 days of starting it` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 9(8)

DECLARE `What my insurer must do about the judgment against me` IS ONE OF
    `it must pay the sum, costs and interest to the Public Trustee as trustee for the person I injured`  -- s 9(1)(b)(i)
    `it must pay the sum, costs and interest directly to the person I injured`                          -- s 9(1)(b)(ii)
    `it may pay, but section 9 does not make it pay: the sum does not exceed the relevant amount`       -- s 9(1)(a)
    `section 9 does not apply to the judgment`                                                         -- s 9(1) gateway fails
    `nothing is payable: my insurer had no notice of the proceedings within 7 days of their start`     -- s 9(6)(a)
    `nothing is payable while enforcement is stayed pending an appeal`                                 -- s 9(6)(b)
    `nothing is payable: the policy was cancelled before the accident and the certificate dealt with`  -- s 9(6)(c)
    `nothing is payable: the court has declared my insurer may avoid the policy`                       -- s 9(7)

GIVEN `the judgment` IS A `The judgment against me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 9 apply to the judgment against me` IF
        `the judgment`'s `a certificate of insurance had been issued for my policy`
    AND `Must my policy cover my liability for this death or injury` (`the judgment`'s `the injury`)
    AND `the judgment`'s `the liability is covered by my policy, or would be but for the insurer's right to avoid or cancel it`
    AND `the judgment`'s `I am a person insured by the policy`

GIVEN `the judgment` IS A `The judgment against me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did my insurer have notice of the proceedings in time` IF
    CONSIDER `the judgment`'s `days after the proceedings began that my insurer had notice of them`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST `days` THEN `days` AT MOST 7

GIVEN `the judgment` IS A `The judgment against me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 9(6)(c) bar payment` IF
        `the judgment`'s `my policy was cancelled before the accident`
    AND `the certificate was dealt with`
    WHERE
        `the certificate was dealt with` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the judgment`'s `the certificate`
            WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the judgment` IS A `The judgment against me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my insurer rely on a declaration that it may avoid the policy` IF
        `the judgment`'s `the court has declared, in an action begun no later than 3 months after the proceedings, that my insurer may avoid the policy for non-disclosure or misrepresentation`
    AND (    NOT `the judgment`'s `the proceedings against me began before the insurer's action`
         OR  `the judgment`'s `my insurer told the claimant of its action, and the ground, within 7 days of starting it`)

GIVEN `the judgment` IS A `The judgment against me`, `the relevant amount in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What my insurer must do about the judgment against me`
DECIDE `What must my insurer do about the judgment against me` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `Does section 9 apply to the judgment against me` `the judgment`
            THEN `section 9 does not apply to the judgment`
        IF NOT `Did my insurer have notice of the proceedings in time` `the judgment`
            THEN `nothing is payable: my insurer had no notice of the proceedings within 7 days of their start`
        IF `the judgment`'s `enforcement is stayed pending an appeal`
            THEN `nothing is payable while enforcement is stayed pending an appeal`
        IF `Does section 9(6)(c) bar payment` `the judgment`
            THEN `nothing is payable: the policy was cancelled before the accident and the certificate dealt with`
        IF `Can my insurer rely on a declaration that it may avoid the policy` `the judgment`
            THEN `nothing is payable: the court has declared my insurer may avoid the policy`
        IF `the judgment`'s `the sum awarded, excluding costs and interest, in dollars` AT MOST `the relevant amount in dollars`
            THEN `it may pay, but section 9 does not make it pay: the sum does not exceed the relevant amount`
        IF     `Is the person I injured a specified person` (`the judgment`'s `the claimant`)
           AND `the judgment`'s `the judgment requires payment to the Public Trustee`
            THEN `it must pay the sum, costs and interest to the Public Trustee as trustee for the person I injured`
        OTHERWISE `it must pay the sum, costs and interest directly to the person I injured`

-- s 9(9): "If the amount which an insurer becomes liable to pay under this section in respect of a liability of a person
-- insured by a policy exceeds the amount for which the insurer would apart from this section be liable under the policy in
-- respect of that liability, the insurer is entitled to recover the excess from that person."
-- For me: whatever s 9 made my insurer pay beyond what my policy obliged it to pay, it can recover from me.
GIVEN `the amount my insurer must pay under section 9 in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount my insurer would owe under the policy apart from section 9 in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much can my insurer recover from me after paying under section 9` IS
    IF   `the amount my insurer must pay under section 9 in dollars` GREATER THAN `the amount my insurer would owe under the policy apart from section 9 in dollars`
    THEN `the amount my insurer must pay under section 9 in dollars` MINUS `the amount my insurer would owe under the policy apart from section 9 in dollars`
    ELSE 0

§§ `10, 12 and 13. If I become bankrupt`

-- s 10(1): where I am insured under a policy issued for the purposes of the Act against liabilities to third parties, then
-- "(a) in the event of the insured becoming bankrupt or making a composition or arrangement with the insured's creditors;
-- or (b) in the case of the insured being a company" (winding up, receiver or manager, debenture holders taking possession),
-- "if either before or after that event any such liability ... is incurred by the insured the insured's rights against the
-- insurer under the policy in respect of the liability are, despite anything in any written law to the contrary, to be
-- transferred to and vest in the third party to whom the liability was so incurred."
-- s 10(2): the same where an order under s 419 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 is made "for the
-- administration in bankruptcy of the estate of a deceased debtor".
-- s 10(6): ss 10-12 "do not apply -- (a) where a company is wound up voluntarily merely for the purposes of reconstruction or
-- of amalgamation ...; or (b) to any case to which section 28(1), (2) and (3) of the Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 ...
-- applies." The WICA case is a borrowed term: a fact.
DECLARE `What happened to me` IS ONE OF
    `I became bankrupt`                                                        -- s 10(1)(a)
    `I made a composition or arrangement with my creditors`                    -- s 10(1)(a)
    `I died and my estate is being administered in bankruptcy`                 -- s 10(2)
    `my company was wound up, other than voluntarily merely to reconstruct or amalgamate` -- s 10(1)(b)(i), (6)(a)
    `my company was wound up voluntarily merely to reconstruct or amalgamate`  -- s 10(6)(a)
    `none of these`

GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened to me`
      `I was insured under a policy issued for the purposes of this Act against the liability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I incurred the liability, before or after the event` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 28 of the Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 applies to the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my rights against my insurer pass to the person I injured` IF
        `the event is one section 10 reaches`
    AND `I was insured under a policy issued for the purposes of this Act against the liability`
    AND `I incurred the liability, before or after the event`
    AND NOT `section 28 of the Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 applies to the case`
    WHERE
        `the event is one section 10 reaches` MEANS
            CONSIDER `what happened`
            WHEN `my company was wound up voluntarily merely to reconstruct or amalgamate` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 12: once I am bankrupt (or my company wound up), "no agreement made between the insurer and the insured after liability
-- has been incurred to a third party and after the commencement of the bankruptcy or winding up ... nor any waiver,
-- assignment or other disposition made by, or payment made to, the insured after the commencement aforesaid is effective to
-- defeat or affect the rights transferred to the third party". The text puts both times on an agreement, and only the
-- second on a waiver, assignment, disposition or payment.
DECLARE `My dealing with my insurer` IS ONE OF
    `an agreement`
    `a waiver, assignment, disposition, or a payment to me`

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A `My dealing with my insurer`
      `made after I incurred the liability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `made after my bankruptcy began` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my dealing with my insurer after my bankruptcy defeat the injured person's rights` IF
    NOT `section 12 strikes it down`
    WHERE
        `section 12 strikes it down` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the dealing`
            WHEN `an agreement` THEN `made after I incurred the liability` AND `made after my bankruptcy began`
            WHEN `a waiver, assignment, disposition, or a payment to me` THEN `made after my bankruptcy began`

-- s 13(1): "Where a certificate of insurance has been issued ..., the happening in relation to any person insured by the
-- policy of any event that is mentioned in section 10(1) or (2) does not, despite anything in this Act, affect any such
-- liability of that person as is required to be covered by a policy under section 4(1)(b)."
-- Where there was no certificate, or the liability is not one s 4(1)(b) requires to be covered, s 13 says nothing and
-- insolvency law decides; the encoding returns NOTHING rather than a guess.
GIVEN `a certificate of insurance was issued for my policy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability is one my policy must cover` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my bankruptcy affect my liability to the person I injured` IS
    IF   `a certificate of insurance was issued for my policy` AND `the liability is one my policy must cover`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `14. Settlement behind the injured person's back`

-- s 14(1): "No settlement by an insurer in respect of any claim which might be made by a third party in respect of any such
-- liability as is required to be covered by a policy under section 4(1)(b) is valid unless the third party is a party to the
-- settlement."  "might be made": the claim need not yet have been brought.
-- s 14(2): "A policy issued under this Act remains in force and available for third parties despite the death of any person
-- insured ... as if the insured person were still alive." Unconditional; not given a rule of its own.
GIVEN `the person I injured is a party to the settlement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my insurer's settlement of the injured person's claim valid` IF
    `the person I injured is a party to the settlement`

§§ `11. Must I say whether I was insured`

-- s 11(1): "Any person against whom a claim is made in respect of any such liability as is required to be covered by a
-- policy under section 4(1)(b) must on demand by or on behalf of the person making the claim state whether or not the person
-- was insured in respect of that liability by any policy having effect for the purposes of this Act or would have been so
-- insured if the insurer had not avoided or cancelled the policy and if the person was or would have been so insured give
-- such particulars with respect to that policy as were specified in the certificate of insurance".
-- s 11(6): "If without reasonable excuse any person fails to comply with this section or wilfully makes any false or
-- misleading statement in reply to any such demand ..., the person shall be guilty of an offence".
DECLARE `What I must tell the claimant` IS ONE OF
    `whether I was insured, and the particulars on the certificate of insurance`
    `that I was not insured`
    `nothing, until the claimant demands it`

DECLARE `The claimant's demand` HAS
    `a claim was made against me for a liability section 4(1)(b) requires to be covered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant, or someone for them, demanded the information`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was insured for that liability`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `I would have been insured had my insurer not avoided or cancelled the policy`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `I said whether I was insured`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `I gave the particulars on the certificate`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `I wilfully made a false or misleading statement`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `I had a reasonable excuse`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the demand` IS A `The claimant's demand`
GIVETH A `What I must tell the claimant`
DECIDE `What must I tell the person claiming against me` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (    `the demand`'s `a claim was made against me for a liability section 4(1)(b) requires to be covered`
                AND `the demand`'s `the claimant, or someone for them, demanded the information`)
            THEN `nothing, until the claimant demands it`
        IF     `the demand`'s `I was insured for that liability`
            OR `the demand`'s `I would have been insured had my insurer not avoided or cancelled the policy`
            THEN `whether I was insured, and the particulars on the certificate of insurance`
        OTHERWISE `that I was not insured`

GIVEN `the demand` IS A `The claimant's demand`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of an offence under section 11` IF
        `I failed to give what I must, or lied`
    AND NOT `the demand`'s `I had a reasonable excuse`
    WHERE
        `I failed to give what I must, or lied` MEANS
            CONSIDER `What must I tell the person claiming against me` `the demand`
            WHEN `nothing, until the claimant demands it` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `that I was not insured` THEN
                    NOT `the demand`'s `I said whether I was insured`
                OR  `the demand`'s `I wilfully made a false or misleading statement`
            WHEN `whether I was insured, and the particulars on the certificate of insurance` THEN
                    NOT `the demand`'s `I said whether I was insured`
                OR  NOT `the demand`'s `I gave the particulars on the certificate`
                OR  `the demand`'s `I wilfully made a false or misleading statement`

§§ `15. Duty to surrender certificate on cancellation of policy`

-- s 15(1): "Where a certificate of insurance has been issued ... and the policy is cancelled by mutual consent or by virtue of
-- any provision in the policy, the person to whom the certificate was issued must, within 7 days from the taking effect of
-- the cancellation, surrender the certificate to the insurer or, if it has been lost or destroyed, make a statutory
-- declaration to that effect."
-- Read with s 9(6)(c): doing this duty on time is one of the things that lets the insurer refuse a later judgment.
DECLARE `Party to section 15` IS ONE OF `the holder of the certificate`
DECLARE `Act under section 15` IS ONE OF `surrender the certificate, or declare it lost or destroyed`

GIVEN `the policy has been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to section 15` `Act under section 15`
DECIDE `my duty to surrender my certificate` IS
    IF   `the policy has been cancelled`
    THEN PARTY `the holder of the certificate`
         MUST  `surrender the certificate, or declare it lost or destroyed`
         WITHIN 7
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the holder of the certificate`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The same duty as a decision, for asking after the event: days after the cancellation took effect on which I surrendered
-- or declared, NOTHING if I have not.
GIVEN `my policy was cancelled after a certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days after the cancellation took effect that I surrendered or declared` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I failed to surrender my certificate in time` IF
        `my policy was cancelled after a certificate was issued`
    AND `not done within 7 days`
    WHERE
        `not done within 7 days` MEANS
            CONSIDER `days after the cancellation took effect that I surrendered or declared`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST `days` THEN `days` GREATER THAN 7

§§ `16. Producing my certificate, and reporting an injury accident`

-- s 16(1): "Any person driving a motor vehicle on a road must on being so required by a police officer give the person's
-- name and address and the name and address of the owner of the motor vehicle and produce his or her certificate."
-- s 16(3): if the driver "within 5 days after the date on which the production of his or her certificate was so required
-- produces the certificate in person at any police office or police station in Singapore that may have been specified by
-- the driver at the time ... the driver must not be convicted of an offence under subsection (2) by reason only of failure to
-- produce his or her certificate to the police officer."
DECLARE `The police request` HAS
    `I was driving on a road and a police officer required it`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `I gave my name and address and the owner's`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `I produced my certificate to the officer`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    -- days after the request on which I produced it in person at a police station I named; NOTHING if I did not
    `days after the request that I produced it at a police station I named`   IS A MAYBE NUMBER

GIVEN `the request` IS A `The police request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of failing to give my details or produce my certificate` IF
        `the request`'s `I was driving on a road and a police officer required it`
    AND (   NOT `the request`'s `I gave my name and address and the owner's`
         OR (    NOT `the request`'s `I produced my certificate to the officer`
             AND NOT `I produced it within 5 days at the station I named`))
    WHERE
        `I produced it within 5 days at the station I named` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the request`'s `days after the request that I produced it at a police station I named`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST `days` THEN `days` AT MOST 5

-- s 16(4): where "an accident occurs involving personal injury to another person" and "the driver of the vehicle does not at
-- the time produce his or her certificate to a police officer or to some person who having reasonable grounds for so doing
-- has required its production, the driver must, as soon as possible and in any case within 24 hours of the occurrence of the
-- accident, report the accident at a police office or police station in Singapore and thereupon produce his or her
-- certificate."  s 16(6): no conviction "by reason only of failure to produce his or her certificate if within 5 days after
-- the occurrence of the accident the person produces the certificate in person at any police office or police station in
-- Singapore that may be specified by him or her at the time the accident was reported."
-- "as soon as possible" is for the court: an input beside the hard 24-hour ceiling.
DECLARE `Party to section 16(4)` IS ONE OF `the driver`
DECLARE `Act under section 16(4)` IS ONE OF `report the accident at a police station and produce the certificate`

GIVEN `the accident injured another person and I did not produce my certificate at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to section 16(4)` `Act under section 16(4)`
DECIDE `my duty to report the accident` IS
    IF   `the accident injured another person and I did not produce my certificate at the time`
    THEN PARTY `the driver`
         MUST  `report the accident at a police station and produce the certificate`
         WITHIN 24
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the driver`
    ELSE FULFILLED

DECLARE `The injury accident` HAS
    `the accident involved personal injury to another person`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `I produced my certificate at the time to a police officer or someone entitled to ask` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- hours after the accident on which I reported it at a police station; NOTHING if I did not
    `hours after the accident that I reported it at a police station`          IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the court accepts I reported as soon as possible`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `I produced my certificate when I reported`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    -- days after the accident on which I produced it in person at a police station I named; NOTHING if I did not
    `days after the accident that I produced it at a police station I named`   IS A MAYBE NUMBER

GIVEN `the accident` IS AN `The injury accident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of failing to report the accident` IF
        `the duty arose`
    AND (   NOT `reported in time`
         OR (    NOT `the accident`'s `I produced my certificate when I reported`
             AND NOT `produced within 5 days at the station I named`))
    WHERE
        `the duty arose` MEANS
                `the accident`'s `the accident involved personal injury to another person`
            AND NOT `the accident`'s `I produced my certificate at the time to a police officer or someone entitled to ask`
        `reported in time` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the accident`'s `hours after the accident that I reported it at a police station`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST `hours` THEN `hours` AT MOST 24 AND `the accident`'s `the court accepts I reported as soon as possible`
        `produced within 5 days at the station I named` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the accident`'s `days after the accident that I produced it at a police station I named`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST `days` THEN `days` AT MOST 5

-- s 16(7): "It is the duty of the owner of a motor vehicle to give any information that the owner may be required by or on
-- behalf of the Deputy Commissioner of Police to give for the purpose of determining whether the motor vehicle was or was
-- not being driven in contravention of section 3 on any occasion when the driver was required under this section to produce
-- his or her certificate." s 16(8): failing to comply is an offence.
GIVEN `the police required information from me as owner about whether the vehicle was driven uninsured` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I gave it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty as owner of failing to give the police information` IF
    `the police required information from me as owner about whether the vehicle was driven uninsured` AND NOT `I gave it`

§§ `Penalties`

-- s 3(2): "a fine not exceeding $1,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 months or ... both".
-- s 11(6), s 15(2), s 16(2), (5), (8): "a fine not exceeding $500 and, in the case of a second or subsequent conviction, to a
-- fine not exceeding $1,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months". No imprisonment on a first conviction.
DECLARE `My offence` IS ONE OF
    `using or permitting use without cover (section 3)`
    `failing to say whether I was insured (section 11)`
    `failing to surrender my certificate (section 15)`
    `failing to give my details or produce my certificate (section 16(2))`
    `failing to report an injury accident (section 16(5))`
    `as owner, failing to give the police information (section 16(8))`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `My offence`, `a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined in dollars` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `using or permitting use without cover (section 3)` THEN 1000
    OTHERWISE IF `a second or subsequent conviction` THEN 1000 ELSE 500

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `My offence`, `a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest I can be imprisoned in months` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `using or permitting use without cover (section 3)` THEN 3
    OTHERWISE IF `a second or subsequent conviction` THEN 6 ELSE 0
